um","abstract":[{"text":"One of the alternatives for Metronome.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLMetronome.Content","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Content-swift.enum","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","abstract":[{"text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"displayed in the music notation.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLMetronome","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBeatUnit":{"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLBeatUnit","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBeatUnit","abstract":[{"text":"The beat-unit group combines elements used repeatedly in the metronome element to specify a note within a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"metronome mark.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MXLBeatUnit","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbeatunit","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLBeatUnit","kind":"identifier"}]}}}